+# Mod Settings on macOS (arm64)
+
+This branch (`macos`) builds Mod Settings (upstream e904815, v0.2.21 + 8 commits) as a RED4ext-macos plugin for the
+native macOS build of Cyberpunk 2077 2.3.1 (binary UUID `A6656ADC-FBE2-36A4-9B9D-B4A9DE645089`). The Windows build
+(top-level `CMakeLists.txt`, cyberpunk_cmake, MSVC) is unchanged: macOS code is behind `#ifdef __APPLE__` or in
+`macos/`. The submodules in `deps/` are not modified.
+
+Evidence: `RE` = `~/Downloads/projects/cet/research/re_modsettings/results.md` (and the decompiles next to it).
+
+## Build
+
+```bash
+export PATH=~/Downloads/projects/cet/tools/venv/bin:$PATH
+cmake -S macos -B build-mac -G Ninja && cmake --build build-mac
+```
+
+Needs `../RED4ext.SDK` (the macOS SDK fork, branch `cet-codeware`; override with `-DRED4EXT_SDK_DIR`). No network.
+
+Output: `build-mac/ModSettings.dylib` and the install layout in `build-mac/package/red4ext/plugins/mod_settings/`:
+
+| file | from |
+| --- | --- |
+| `ModSettings.dylib` | this build |
+| `Scripts/packed.reds`, `Scripts/module.reds` | `src/redscript`, packed by `deps/cpcmake/scripts/PackFiles.cmake` and `Module.reds.in`, as `configure_redscript` does |
+| `ModSettings.archive` | `src/wolvenkit/packed/archive/pc/mod/` (identical to the v0.2.21 release) |
+| `ModSettings.archive.xl` | `src/archiveXL/` |
+| `readme.md`, `license.md` | repo root |
+
+The folder name stays `mod_settings` (as on Windows), so `user.ini` stays at `red4ext/plugins/mod_settings/user.ini`.
+The RED4ext-macos launcher (`scripts/launch_red4ext.sh`) compiles each plugin's `Scripts/` folder with the game's
+`scc` when `red4ext_plugin_check` passes for the plugin. `packed.reds` compiles with redscript-cli 0.5.31 against the
+2.3.1 vanilla bundle. (redscript 1.0 preview rejects it with LESS_VISIBLE_OVERRIDE errors; so does the v0.2.21 release.)
+
+## Changes
+
+### Build and platform
+
+| file | change |
+| --- | --- |
+| `macos/CMakeLists.txt` | Builds the dylib (`RED4EXT_PLATFORM_MACOS`, `-undefined dynamic_lookup`, hidden visibility) and stages the install layout. `Scripting/RTTIRegistrar.cpp` is not built: it is dead code upstream and calls `RTTIRegistrator::Add`, which the SDK no longer has. |
+| `macos/include/ModSettingsMac.hpp` | Force-included. v1 API aliases (as Input Loader), `ScriptInstance = void*` (as CET-mac), empty `__fastcall`, RedLib first, platform helper declarations, the 3 macOS-only address hashes. |
+| `macos/src/MacPlatform.cpp` | `_NSGetExecutablePath`, game root = executable up 4 levels, plugin folder by `dladdr`, game image base (the `MH_EXECUTE` image, not image 0), `__DATA_CONST` pointer swap, 4-byte `__TEXT` patch (`mach_vm_protect` RW+COPY, write, RX, `sys_icache_invalidate`, as CET-mac). Both write only after the current value matches. |
+| `macos/include/Registrar.hpp` | Replaces cpcmake's: resolves the hash in `Load()` (not in a static initializer with `GetModuleHandle` subtraction), attaches with `sdk->hooking->Attach` at the absolute address, logs and skips a hash that does not resolve (Windows retried forever). |
+| `macos/include/CyberpunkMod.hpp` | `TimeTracker` on `std::chrono::steady_clock` instead of `QueryPerformanceCounter`. |
+| `macos/include/ArchiveXL.hpp` | Plugin folder by `dladdr` instead of `GetModuleFileNameW`. The `Memory::Vault` readiness check is dropped: `Memory_Vault` is wrong and unverified in the macOS DB (SDK `docs/ADDRESS_AUDIT.md`), and referencing it makes the gate refuse the plugin. The facade call path is unchanged. |
+| `macos/include/RED4ext/Scripting/Natives/userRuntimeSettingsVar.hpp`, `userSettingsVar.hpp` | jackhumbert SDK headers the macOS SDK lacks. See "RuntimeSettingsVar" below. |
+| `macos/include/RedLib.hpp`, `macos/vendor/RedLib`, `macos/vendor/nameof` | RedLib from `cp2077-codeware-mac` 3f011a5 `lib/Red` (the ArchiveXL-macos copy with its macOS fixes: explicit definition instantiation, clang scoped-enum names, non-const `IsEqual`). `deps/red_lib` (jack branch) targets the older SDK and does not build. nameof is the same single header as Codeware-mac. MIT licenses copied. |
+| `Main.cpp` | `DllMain` becomes `__attribute__((constructor))`. Base-address log uses the game image. Legacy cleanup keeps the 4 exact Windows paths (`r6/scripts/mod_settings`, `archive/pc/mod/ModSettings.archive`, `.archive.xl`, `ModSettings.xl`); it runs only if `<root>/r6` exists, deletes a folder only where a folder is expected and a file only where a file is expected (no `remove_all` on the archive paths). `scripts->Add` registers `<plugin>/Scripts` (bookkeeping, as Codeware-mac). Installs the two input-manager changes below. |
+| `Utils.cpp` | `GetRootDir` = executable up 4. `ToWString` (unused) via `std::filesystem` (wchar_t is UTF-32 here). |
+| `Utils.hpp` | `RedTypeFromString<T>` looks fundamental types up by name (`Bool`, `Int32`, ...): the Windows code reads their vtables by address hash (`RTTITYPE`), and those hashes are not in the macOS DB. Specializations made `inline`. |
+| `ModSettings.cpp` | `fopen` with the UTF-8 path instead of `_wfopen`. Listener calls with arguments build `StackArgs_t` (the SDK only has the variadic overload for a class context). `Handle<IScriptable>` built explicitly. Platform-neutral fix: C-API registration took a unique lock while holding the shared lock on the same mutex (never returns); it now takes one unique lock. |
+| `Variable.cpp`, `ModConfigVar.hpp`, `ScriptProperty.hpp` | SDK API drift: `DynArray::size` -> `std::ranges::size`, `CreateInstance()` + cast, `IType::FromString(void*, const CString&)` through one `TypeFromString` helper, `WeakHandle` compare by instance. `static_assert` that `runtimeVar` is at +0x40 in every config var class. |
+| `ActionNameEx.hpp` | The macOS SDK's `ink::ActionName` has no named fields; `ToName` reads the CName at +0x40 (native `inkActionName::IsAction` 0x1048ABDD0 reads it there). |
+| `ScriptDefinitions.hpp` | `EScriptType : int32_t` (was `long`, 8 bytes on LP64; the game reads a u32 at +0x2C). `__unaligned __declspec(align(1))` dropped (offset 0x58 is aligned anyway). Offset asserts. Comment: the `ScriptDefinition` virtual list is MSVC-shaped and is never called. |
+| `ScriptData.hpp` | macOS tail: `SharedSpinLock` 0x130, `pthread_mutex_t` 0x138, size 0x178 (RE, Codeware-mac `ScriptBundle.hpp`). Only `classes` (0xD0) is read. |
+
+### RuntimeSettingsVar (game ABI)
+
+Mod Settings creates its own `user::RuntimeSettingsVar` subclasses and hands them to the game through the
+`ConfigVar` script classes; the game's `userSettingsVar` natives call their virtuals. Under clang the destructor takes
+two slots, so every later slot moves by +8 compared to MSVC. The macOS header declares `virtual ~RuntimeSettingsVar()`
+in slot 1, which yields exactly the game's layout. Checked against the 2.3.1 binary:
+
+| native (Mac address) | runtime var access |
+| --- | --- |
+| `userSettingsVar::WasModifiedSinceLastSave` 0x10489D038 | vt+0x18 |
+| `userSettingsVar::HasRequestedValue` 0x10489D078 | vt+0x20 |
+| `userSettingsVar::RestoreDefault` 0x10489D0B8 | vt+0x30, w1 = 2 |
+| RuntimeSettingsVarBool setter 0x101E5C1A8 | vt+0x38 (SetRequestedValue) |
+| `GetName` / `GetGroupPath` / `GetDisplayName` / `GetDisplayNameKeysSize` / `GetType` / `GetUpdatePolicy` / `IsInPreGame` / `GetOrder` | +0x08 / +0x10 / +0x18 / +0x2C / +0x40 / +0x41 / +0x44 / +0x48 |
+
+`clang -fdump-vtable-layouts` on the built classes gives the same slots (WasModified 0x18, HasChange 0x20,
+RestoreDefault 0x30, SetRequestedValue 0x38). Data offsets are asserted in the header.
+
+### Addresses and hooks
+
+| Windows hash | use | macOS | evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 3702071356 UserMapping::GetMappingCollection | call | 1:0x1D796B4 (returns nullptr on a miss) | RE, confirmed |
+| 4196866905 UserMapping::ClearRuntimeDataOnRawMappings | call | 1:0x1D7923C | RE, confirmed |
+| 3993832650 ReleaseScriptData | hook (before) | 1:0x21ECFD8 (ScriptBundle dtor, already in the DB; Codeware-mac hooks it too, RED4ext chains hooks) | RE, re_boot |
+| 2583235069 CalcHash | inlined | reimplemented: `h = h*31 + (int8)c`, seed 0 (`Hooks/ApplyOverrides.hpp`) | RE (parser 0x101D853B4) |
+| 1773342692 ApplyOverrides | hook | vtable slot swap, see below | RE, likely |
+| 3298233196 SkipKey | hook | inlined; one-instruction patch, see below | RE |
+
+New macOS-only DB entries (hash = FNV-1a 32 of the name, the Codeware-mac / ArchiveXL-macos convention):
+
+| name | hash | offset |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| ModSettings_InputManager_ApplyOverridesSlot | 647509972 | 2:0x1B45F0 (0x106F945F0) |
+| ModSettings_InputManager_ApplyOverridesThunk | 3781755204 | 1:0x1D735A4 |
+| ModSettings_KeyBindingListen_PadSkipBranch | 1325863745 | 1:0x48039B4 |
+
+They are in `RED4ext.SDK/cyberpunk2077_addresses.json` (commit on `cet-codeware`), applied with
+`tools/re/apply_overlay.py` from `research/re_modsettings/modsettings_address_overlay.json` and
+`modsettings_macos_overlay.json`.
+
+- **ApplyOverrides.** The `game::input::Manager` function is an 8-byte thunk (`ldr x0,[x0,#0x10]; b 0x101D5C774`)
+  directly followed by the revert thunk, so an inline hook would corrupt the neighbour. Both callers dispatch through
+  vtable slot +0x258. `InstallInputManagerHooks` reads the slot and swaps it only if it holds the thunk resolved from
+  the DB (the file's chained fixup for 0x106F945F0 targets 0x1D735A4). `ApplyOverrides_Original` keeps the thunk.
+  Unload restores the slot.
+- **SkipKey.** Inlined into the key-binding listen lambda 0x1048038B8. Pad keys 0..5 are remapped to IK_Escape, pad
+  keys 6..0x13 are skipped by `b.hi 0x10480392C` at 0x1048039B4. The patch retargets it to the accept path 0x1048039DC
+  (`0x54FFFBC8` -> `0x54000148`), so pad keys 6..0x13 are stored with their own code, as on Windows (where SkipKey
+  returns false for every pad key after the same remap). If the word is not `0x54FFFBC8`, nothing is written and the
+  log says so. Unload reverts it.
+
+Gate: `red4ext_plugin_check RED4ext.SDK/cyberpunk2077_addresses.json ModSettings.dylib` prints OK. Every DB hash
+compiled into the dylib is verified.
+
+## Untested
+
+Nothing has run in game. Check in a logging run (`red4ext/logs/mod_settings-*.log`):
+
+- "Hook ReleaseScriptData attached", "ApplyOverrides: hooked the input manager vtable slot", "SkipKey: patched".
+- "Loaded <Class>.<prop>" lines for installed mods, the Mod Settings menu entry in the main and pause menus, and the
+  localized labels (the archive and `.archive.xl` go through ArchiveXL's facade, queued until ArchiveXL registers
+  its RTTI class).
+- Accept: `user.ini` written to `red4ext/plugins/mod_settings/user.ini` (`.bak` next to it) and read back on the next
+  start.
+- Key bindings: a mod's EInputKey setting overrides its `overridableUI` mapping after Accept and after a restart; pad
+  buttons other than A/B/X/Y/Start/Back can be bound. The patch also applies to the game's own key-binding screen, as
+  the Windows hook did.
+- `ApplyOverrides` slot confidence is "likely" (RE): all callers and semantics match, but there is no Windows binary
+  to diff against.
+- The `__TEXT` patch briefly makes one code page non-executable; it runs once at plugin load (same method as CET-mac).
